# DotNetFrameworkMigrationUtility
A Command-Line Tool to assist in the migration from .NET Framework 4.5 to .NET Standard 2.0 and .NET Core 3.0

In .NET Core 3.0, Microsoft introduced a new cross-platform base class library referred to as .NET Standard 2.0. The .NET Standard is a formal specification of .NET APIs that are intended to be available on all .NET runtimes.

For .NET Framework 4.5, it has many APIs that are not included in .NET Standard 2.0 and will cause build errors unless you change your project to target .NET Standard 2.0.

This command-line tool migrates your project from .NET Framework 4.5 (or higher) to .NET Standard 2.0, making it easier for developers to start developing for .NET Core 3.0.

## Installation/Usage

1. Clone or download this repository.
2. Open a command prompt and navigate to the root directory of the downloaded (or cloned) project.
3. Run the following command in the command prompt: `DotNetFrameworkMigrationUtility.exe -s "C:\path\to\your\project\*.csproj"`
4. Replace `"C:\path\to\your\project\*.csproj"` with the path to your .csproj file or directory.

## Disclaimer

Please be aware that this is a basic tool and may not cover all possible migration scenarios. Use it as a starting point, help it guide you through your projects, and customize as per your requirements. Also, be aware that running migrations have the potential to introduce breaking changes. Please back up your projects before running automigrations.

Also keep in mind that .NET Core can be a paradigm shift from .NET Framework, as they are significantly different technologies. The tool does not cover .NET Framework to .NET Core porting, it focuses on changes from .NET Framework 4.5 to .NET Standard 2.0. 

## Contributing

Please read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://gist.com/CONTRIBUTING.md) for details on our code of--------------------            //@@@   Debug.Assert(PexHelpers.IsTrueForAllSubjects(() => 
